01:24:17.480 --> 01:24:19.820
1997 Winston. The Winston is a

01:24:19.820 --> 01:24:21.660
unique event to NASCAR Winston Cup racing

01:24:21.660 --> 01:24:23.300
because it's broken into three segments.

01:24:23.800 --> 01:24:26.160
Two 30-lap segments followed by a 10-lap

01:24:26.160 --> 01:24:28.100
shootout. And we'll make adjustments in between.

01:24:29.000 --> 01:24:29.860
We know about wedge.

01:24:30.510 --> 01:24:35.460
changing the weight on each tire. We know about panned rods. Lowering the panned rod makes the

01:24:35.460 --> 01:24:41.940
car tighter. Raising the panned rod makes the car looser. We'll also use tire pressure. Dropping

01:24:41.940 --> 01:24:46.340
the tire pressure or raising the tire pressure by as little as one pound can make a big difference

01:24:46.340 --> 01:24:53.250
in the tire's spring rate. We'll use spring rubbers. Putting a piece of rubber in a spring

01:24:53.250 --> 01:24:59.090
or pulling it out of a spring can make that spring stiffer or softer by as much as 25%.

01:25:00.890 --> 01:25:03.610
But what's really different about this year than all the years past?

01:25:04.170 --> 01:25:06.130
Well, NASCAR's made an aerodynamic rule change.

01:25:06.320 --> 01:25:10.420
They've made us take the fenders from 76 inches wide to 74 inches wide.

01:25:10.560 --> 01:25:12.580
That's taking front downforce away from the cars.

01:25:13.100 --> 01:25:18.290
To get that downforce back, you're going to see a lot of guys putting more and more tape on as the night goes on.

01:25:18.800 --> 01:25:21.490
